    "code_released": "not stated",
    "peer_reviewed": "preprint",
    "problems": "The study does not test the claim's direction or intervention. Its authors note that the reversion proxy is operational rather than an observed ancestor; the training intervention is not a formal mediation analysis and may change other coordinates; several random-axis blocks also reduce harmfulness; and the results concern selected models, layers, tasks, prompts, and judges.",
    "rows_left_out": "No additional rows from the paper's geometric trajectory scores, local vocabulary derivatives, utility metrics, late-layer sweep, random-axis controls, or judge robustness were included: these concern the distinct reversion direction, local lexical derivatives rather than generated refusal rates, or other outcomes, and do not test any listed claim version. The main cross-model unsafe-rate intervention results and the rehearsal safety results are retained above.",
    "untested": [
